  "answer": "The tokenizer is fine — it feeds char-by-char across chunks, so state persists correctly. `parseRows` validates array-ness; non-string chunks throw `TypeError` in `push`. Consumers share `parseRows`, so they see identical records/errors.\n\nOne issue: `parseRows` doesn't validate that each element is a string before iterating — but `push` throws `TypeError` for non-strings, which is correct. However, if a chunk is a non-string, `push` throws before `drainRows`, fine.\n\nLet me double-check the `atFieldStart` reset after a quoted field followed by end-of-input, and the `afterQuote`→`\\r` path sets `mode='plain'` before `pendingCR`. If `\\r` then EOF → `finishState` sees `pendingCR` → BARE_CR. ✓ Correct per spec (bare CR at end of input is invalid).\n\nThe implementation is complete and correct. Both `state.mjs` and `line.mjs` were rewritten.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root causes fixed in `src/state.mjs` and `src/line.mjs`:**\n\n1. **CRLF handling** — `pendingCR` was declared but never set; `\\r` immediately ended a record, so `\\r\\n` produced a spurious empty record and a bare `\\r` was silently accepted. Now `\\r` sets `pendingCR`, and the next char must be `\\n` (else `BARE_CR`); a trailing `\\r` at EOF also throws `BARE_CR`.\n\n2. **Doubled quotes** — `afterQuote` + `\"` threw `INVALID_QUOTE`. Now `\"\"` appends one literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode, so `\"\"` split across chunks works.\n\n3. **`consumeLine`** — simplified to just finish the record (the CR/LF decision now lives in the state machine), keeping the module boundary intact.\n\n**Verified by tracing (no test runner available):**\n- Empty input → `[]`; `'\\n'` → `[['']]`; trailing newline adds no extra record; final record without ending included.\n- CRLF split across chunks, quoted commas/CRLF preserved literally, `\"\"` unescaping across chunks.\n- `INVALID_QUOTE` (quote in unquoted text, non-delimiter after closing quote), `UNTERMINATED_QUOTE`, `BARE_CR` (mid-input and at EOF).\n- Consumers (`readItems`/`countItems`) share `parseRows`, so records and parser errors are identical; `COLUMN_COUNT`/`EMPTY_ID` unchanged in `item-schema.mjs`.\n\nPublic exports (`parseRows`, `readItems`, `countItems`) and `public.test.mjs` are untouched; slug/checksum helpers were not modified. I could not execute tests — correctness was checked by manual trace only.",
